  "implementation": [
    "Private NumberBytes abstraction retains scalar decoded-iterator tail validation; contiguous SliceBytes validates fixed-size byte blocks only after overflow when diagnostics require complete syntax classification. Safe as_chunks arrays permit vector reduction; non-digits still override overflow/underflow. No-error overflow remains a short circuit.",
    "Signed slice parser routes positive nonzero inputs to the existing unsigned magnitude accumulator bounded by the SIGNED positive maximum. Negative and zero-prefixed inputs retain the original generic signed path. This benefits the numeric public API and existing positive Content-Range fields without changing wrappers or moving policy to C++."
  ],
  "api_safety": [
    "All existing Rust slice/iterator, production C ABI and historical CXX interfaces unchanged. Shared safe core still forbids unsafe code. No allocations or new dependencies.",
    "FFI raw output writes, byte borrow lifetimes, aliases, null-empty input, uninitialized output storage, output/error mutation and C++ unsigned enum checks are unchanged.",
    "Current parse_number.h corrected implementation prose, shared http_util.cc, HSTS sources, Range core/FFI and accepted Range methods are byte-identical to pre-optimization snapshot.",
    "Frozen numeric/Range/HSTS references, benchmark inputs, loops, cases and descriptors are unchanged. Original historical evidence remains immutable."
  ],
